WHERE

WHERE filters rows based on a condition.

Example:

SELECT *
FROM Student
WHERE age > 20;


WHERE EXISTS

EXISTS checks whether another query returns at least one row.

Syntax:

SELECT ...
FROM table1
WHERE EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM table2
    WHERE ...
);

Why SELECT 1?

You could write
SELECT *
or
SELECT order_id
or
SELECT customer_id
or
SELECT 100
They all work.



Rule of thumb

Use WHERE when filtering by column values.

WHERE salary > 50000

Use EXISTS when asking "Does at least one matching row exist?"

